        "eyebrow": "Science · Two of five",
        "heading": "How we formulate",
        "standfirst": "<p><em>The thinking behind what goes in, and what stays out.</em></p>",
        "intro": "<p>Every ingredient in a Biotaderm product has to earn its place. If it does not do a job the published evidence supports, it does not go in. If a claim cannot be supported by that evidence, it does not go on the label. That single rule keeps the formulas short, the range small, and the copy honest, and it is why you will not find a long list of on-trend extracts here doing very little.</p><p>What you will find is a small number of ingredient types chosen to work together, in a base built to be gentle. The idea running through all of it is the same one that runs through the rest of the brand. Support, not control.</p>",
        "hero_image_alt": "Cold-pressed oil in a beaker on the bench",
